- The sandbox application. Runs untrusted code, talks to the host only by
- postMessage. Knows nothing about Giper Baza, the network or user keys.
- @see ../ARCHITECTURE.md section 4

$bog_vmap_scene $mol_view
	sub /
		- The canvas ground. Inside the frame since the frame stopped being see
		- through: a `color-scheme` is what gives a frame its base colour, and
		- without one Chrome keeps the frame transparent only until the transform
		- on `Stage` promotes it to its own layer, then washes it pale. Declaring
		- the scheme fixes the tone and makes the frame opaque, so anything that
		- has to be under the document has to be in here with it.
		-
		- Still not transformed, and that is the point of section 8: the camera
		- moves the lines by recomputing the `d` of the path, so a stroke stays one
		- pixel at any zoom. Exactly one CSS transform in the system, and it is on
		- `Stage`, not here.
		<= Grid $bog_vmap_scene_grid
			shift <= grid_shift $mol_vector_2d<number> /
				0
				0
			scale <= grid_scale $mol_vector_2d<number> /
				1
				1
		<= Stage $mol_view
			style *
				transform <= camera_transform \none
			sub <= stage /$mol_view_content
	-
	- Stated wait instead of an empty canvas: a cold pack is 2.25 MB and 610 ms,
	- and a blank frame for that long reads as a breakage.
	Wait $mol_view
		sub /
			<= pack_note \
